{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:27:45Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 87, "kind": "tool_use", "text": "Write", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "tool_use", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01WwMNASPxtmfiNTqsHdxHAZ", "input": {"file_path": "/home/dev/projects/test-project/docs/spec.md", "content": "# Spec: Search tasks by title\n\n**Taiga:** #11\n**Type:** Feature\n**Branch:** feature/tp-11/search-tasks-by-title\n\n## Goal\n\nLet me type into a search box to narrow the visible task list down to tasks\nwhose title matches what I typed, so a long list stays usable.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. **Given** tasks exist, **when** I type text into the search input,\n   **then** only tasks whose title contains that text remain visible in the\n   list.\n2. **Given** I type text in a different case than the title (e.g. \"MEET\"\n   against a task titled \"Team meeting\"), **when** filtering runs, **then**\n   it still matches \u2014 matching is case-insensitive.\n3. **Given** the search matches a substring anywhere in the title (not just\n   the start), **when** filtering runs, **then** the task is shown \u2014 e.g.\n   \"meet\" matches \"Team meeting\".\n4. **Given** a state filter (Open/Done/All) is active and I also type a\n   search term, **when** both are active, **then** the list shows only\n   tasks that satisfy *both* \u2014 the same task-list array is narrowed by\n   state first, then by title, exactly as `visibleTasks` already narrows by\n   state in `frontend/src/App.jsx:29`. Search and state filter combine with\n   AND, never override or reset each other.\n5. **Given** my search term matches zero tasks under the current state\n   filter, **when** the list would otherwise render, **then** an explicit\n   message says nothing matched the search \u2014 distinct from the existing\n   \"Nothing to do yet.\" / \"Nothing open right now.\" / \"Nothing done yet.\"\n   copy in `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx:3-7`, which means \"this\n   state filter is empty,\" not \"your search found nothing.\"\n6. **Given** I clear the search input back to empty, **when** filtering\n   runs, **then** all tasks reappear (subject only to the state filter).\n7. **Given** the task list re-fetches after an add/complete/delete/edit\n   (`refresh()` in `App.jsx:16`), **when** the refresh completes, **then**\n   my typed search term is not cleared \u2014 it behaves like `filter`, which\n   already survives refreshes because both live in `App` state, not in\n   fetched data.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- No backend involvement. The state filter has no server-side support today\n  \u2014 `store.list()` (`backend/app/store.py:51`) always returns everything,\n  and `App.jsx` narrows it client-side. Search follows the same pattern:\n  no new query param, no new endpoint, no changes under `backend/`.\n- No fuzzy or typo-tolerant matching. Literal case-insensitive substring\n  only, per the request's own wording (\"case-insensitive... what is\n  actually displayed\").\n- No matching against fields other than the displayed title \u2014 not `id`,\n  not `priority`.\n- No highlighting of the matched substring inside the title.\n- No debouncing/throttling the input. The store is in-memory with no\n  pagination, and filtering is a synchronous array pass over data already\n  in memory \u2014 the same cost the state-filter buttons already pay on every\n  click.\n- No persistence of the search term across a page reload. It is transient\n  UI state, same lifecycle as `filter` (`App.jsx:14`), which also doesn't\n  persist today.\n- Does not change sort order \u2014 the existing high-priority-first sort\n  (`App.jsx:35-37`) still applies to whatever the combined filters leave.\n\n## Affected areas\n\n- `frontend/src/App.jsx` \u2014 add a `search` state value alongside `filter`\n  (line 14); extend the `visibleTasks` filter (lines 29-33) to also test\n  the title; pass `search`/`setSearch` to the new search input and down to\n  `TaskList`.\n- `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx` \u2014 `EMPTY_COPY` (lines 3-7) is\n  keyed only by `filter`; needs a search-aware empty-state message per AC5.\n- A new component under `frontend/src/components/` for the search input\n  itself (placement/naming is a UX decision \u2014 it's a text input, not a\n  toggle-button group, so it doesn't belong inside the existing\n  `TaskFilter.jsx`, which renders `role=\"group\"` buttons).\n- `frontend/src/App.css` \u2014 styling for the new input, likely extending\n  `.list-toolbar` (`App.css:33`) where `TaskFilter` and `ClearCompleted`\n  already sit.\n- No changes to `backend/` (see Non-goals).\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- **Empty store (no tasks at all):** falls through to the existing\n  per-filter empty copy, not the new \"no search matches\" copy \u2014 there's\n  nothing to have searched yet. Distinguish \"0 tasks total\" from \"0 tasks\n  after search narrowed a non-empty list.\"\n- **Search text with no tasks matching, under `filter=all` vs `open` vs\n  `done`:** the \"no matches\" message applies in all three combinations\n  (AC4 + AC5 together).\n- **Whitespace-only search term:** should not throw or behave oddly;\n  treating it as matching everything (empty-after-trim behaves like no\n  search) is a reasonable default consistent with typical search-box UX.\n- **Special characters in the search term** (e.g. `(`, `*`, `.`): must be\n  treated as literal text to match, not a regex \u2014 a title containing\n  literal `(` should be findable by typing `(`, and typing regex\n  metacharacters must never throw.\n- **Search term longer than any title, or containing characters no title\n  has:** zero matches, same \"no matches\" message as AC5.\n- **Clearing search while a state filter is still active:** returns to\n  exactly the state-filtered list (AC6), not the unfiltered full list.\n\n## Open questions\n\nNone \u2014 the request is unambiguous enough to proceed on the defaults stated\nabove (substring match, AND-combine with the state filter, transient\nclient-side state). Exact placement and copy for the search input and the\nnew empty-state message are UX decisions for the next stage, not product\ndecisions requiring sign-off.\n"}, "session_id": "5634ab21-39d3-4140-8e25-a39059160a4a"}}
